2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:02:05-08:00","id":1190734,"title":"","content":"No comments to make right now, I'd strongly recommend listening to section two of the <a href=\"http://www.revolutionspodcast.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Revolutions Podcast</b></a> by <i>Mike Duncan</i>. Mike's done 15 episodes detailing the American Revolution and like everything he lays his hands on, they are excellent! Starts <a href=\"http://www.revolutionspodcast.com/2014/02/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and ends <a href=\"http://www.revolutionspodcast.com/2014/05/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:04:28-08:00","id":1190735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution#post1190729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's pointed as defying moment of Free Council.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:14:42-08:00","id":1190739,"title":"","content":"The Revolution is a major part of Hunter's backstory in Philadelphia, as the sudden upending of decades of British rule changed the paradigms across the colonies. In Philadelphia, the city was already a hunter stronghold, and the Revolution helped to create a kind of &quot;formal&quot; method of hunters working together under the Candle Compact. So not only do you have the typical hunter contests of man vs monster, you have patriots vs loyalists and the spiritual ideas of the Native Americans being destroyed as the Europeans keep advancing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:47:20-08:00","id":1190749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution?p=1190735#post1190735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Positions section of Free Council book:<br /> <b>Minuteman (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Any Libertine who agrees to fight (in some Consilii even just figuratively) may customarily be called a minuteman. In practice, however, only a Libertine who has actually fought on behalf of the order enjoys the benefits of added respect from the citizenry. <br /> Minutemen, obviously, are fashioned on the guerilla militiamen of the American Revolution. The image of the common colonial man summoned out of his house in the middle of the night to defend against the redcoats is not too far off from what a Libertine minuteman actually is. A minuteman is expected to come when his cell phone rings or the strategos calls out to him through telepathy. Minutemen pull on their boots and convene in empty parking lots at four in the morning because a Seer pylon has found someone\u2019s sanctum. They drive to the Assembly site when a mage needs to be escorted out of town. These are the citizen soldiers of the Free Council, and they are all volunteers.<br /> <br /> <b>Letter Carrier (\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> The so-called letter carriers exist in only a few Consilii nowadays. Letter carriers are, to a large extent, emissaries, but nostalgia and a history of sacrifice lend them an aura of additional prestige. In casual language, a letter carriermay be any emissary who travels abroad to carry a message on behalf of the order. Historically, a letter carrier is specifically an emissary who allows his memory to altered with Mind spells so that even the courier himself may not have access to the message. In a few areas, where the <br /> Free Council was especially paranoid about Seer surveillance, letter carriers were even ensorceled into believing they were traveling for their own reasons, not on order business. Some letter carriers may still be carrying around hidden messages in their psyches and not even know it until the mental barriers isolating the message from their own memories begin to erode.<br /> <br /> The position of letter carrier started as little more than a local custom and a nickname somewhere in the Eastern <br /> United States around the late 1930s. During the thick of the cold war, when paranoia was in fashion, letter carriers were more common throughout the United States. Today, they\u2019ve gone the way of the milkman in most Consilii. The majority of Libertines who still identify themselves as letter carriers are in their 60s or 70s now and keep the title out of nostalgia more than anything else. But the title <br /> still carries an aura of old-fashioned dedication.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:23:49-08:00","id":1190765,"title":"","content":"The use of the word &quot;fashioned&quot; would say to me that the Minutemen is inspired by the traditions of Revolution, not a continuation of them. More likely a modern inspiration drawing on the Revolutionary past to create magical sympathy with the modern Council's actions, especially since the Revolution ended before the Nameless War and way before the Free Council existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T15:23:26-08:00","id":1190820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution#post1190729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I have very large problem in <i>not</i> seeing Nameless shaping what will be Free Council of USA in American Revolution. What. suddenly all future Nameless gone 'puff', and hiberante be 20 years, waiting for the proper Nameless War to start?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that a lot of the revolutionary ideas were still not terribly well developed at the time. I mean, I know it's a simplification, but the old &quot;no taxation without representation&quot; is a very legalistic slogan for a revolution. They call King George a tyrant, they don't say that a monarchy is an inherently monstrous system. Most famously, a lot of the founders seem to have thought slavery was wrong, but choose not to really do much about it. My impression is that despite it's success, the revolution ultimately left the existing power structures more or less intact.<br /> <br /> However, those ideas do go on to influence the French and then in turn the Haitian Revolutions where they do radically overturn the old power structures, and in far violent fashion.<br /> <br /> We could do something similar with the Nameless by developing the ideas in Boston Unveiled. I believe it mentions that the consilia in America were subordinate to European consilia. So the Stone Assembly in Boston still bent the knee to Cambridge in England right up to the revolution when they cut ties. Now, 2e has convocations that makes more sense. Presumably Boston was overseen by a British Convocation.<br /> <br /> So perhaps proto-nameless elements in the Diamond were pushing for the Colonial consilia to cut their ties with their convocations. Maybe some of them thought that would make the consilia less oligarchic and more democratic. However, when the dust settled, people like the Stone Assembly were still in charge.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be a part of the Nameless War, more like a prelude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:14:05-08:00","id":1190956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution?p=1190820#post1190820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that a lot of the revolutionary ideas were still not terribly well developed at the time. I mean, I know it's a simplification, but the old &quot;no taxation without representation&quot; is a very legalistic slogan for a revolution. They call King George a tyrant, they don't say that a monarchy is an inherently monstrous system. Most famously, a lot of the founders seem to have thought slavery was wrong, but choose not to really do much about it. My impression is that despite it's success, the revolution ultimately left the existing power structures more or less intact.</div> </div> </div> </div>After this video of 'Real Life Hamilton' I cannot see King George as real Tyrant. Rather Tyrant-Grandpa. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Great video to see Imperialism of Georgian Era England of this times )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rgiyq7rqWhg\" data-code=\"Rgiyq7rqWhg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Rgiyq7rqWhg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:30:57-08:00","id":1190990,"title":"","content":"And to return to the main topic...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution?p=1190820#post1190820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So perhaps proto-nameless elements in the Diamond were pushing for the Colonial consilia to cut their ties with their convocations. Maybe some of them thought that would make the consilia less oligarchic and more democratic. However, when the dust settled, people like the Stone Assembly were still in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diamond Orders members <i>cannot</i> be Nameless, just by definition. Nameless, called then Nephandi, where what now is mostly called Apostates - mages outside of proper Orders alliances, sometimes in Nameless Cults ( / Orders ).<br /> <br /> Thinking about American Revolution impact on Awakened society I would point this:<br /> 1. <b>Rise of Adamantine Arrow in Diamond Orders at large</b> - it's the <i>War</i> of Independence, in the end. Seers connected with British Empire are attacking Diamond in battle.<br /> 2. <b>Destruction of transcontinental relations between Diamond and Seers Orders members.</b> So New York Silver Ladder caucus stops to answer to the 'higher-ups' in London.<br /> 3. <b>Rise of Nameless mages in numbers on general, from the chaos of War in Sleepers society. </b>Weaken Diamond as organisation means more freshly Awakened are not recruited by using Labirynth, Cryptopoly or other typical mechanism. Those left alone new mages are more prone to rebel to authority of Orders in general - and so risen in times of Sleepers revolution - have stron antiauthoritarian views, building proper Nameless Movement and passing Revolution from Sleepers to Awakened society at dawn of 19th century, with information about French Revolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution?p=1190820#post1190820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could do something similar with the Nameless by developing the ideas in Boston Unveiled. I believe it mentions that the consilia in America were subordinate to European consilia. So the Stone Assembly in Boston still bent the knee to Cambridge in England right up to the revolution when they cut ties. Now, 2e has convocations that makes more sense. Presumably Boston was overseen by a British Convocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see in Diamond Orders of Americas to start they own Convocations in times of Revolution and broke their connection with Old World. At least in name. But remember that both Mysterium and Silver Ladder are - literally - world spannig plans for world (occult) domination. Mysterium members even share their GLOBAL soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-02-2018, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:49:36-08:00","id":1190998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190729-dark-eras-american-revolution?p=1190990#post1190990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diamond Orders members <i>cannot</i> be Nameless, just by definition. Nameless, called then Nephandi, where what now is mostly called Apostates - mages outside of proper Orders alliances, sometimes in Nameless Cults ( / Orders ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nefandi. Nephandi is Ascension. More to the point, I said proto-Nameless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:44:05-08:00","id":1191087,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for inspirational ideas, Rogue Games's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/201966/Colonial-Gothic-Rulebook-3rd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Colonial Gothic</a> RPG is fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T19:13:14-08:00","id":1191199,"title":"","content":"Expending my predictions on American Revolution mages society into proper Nameless War...<br /> 4. ( It's more guessing but based on 2E gameline material ) <b>Creation of Nameless as 19th century faction.</b> At the start, Nameless were group of Nameless Cults (Orders) inner fighting groups fighting with Diamond, Seers or even themselves. It's more accurate to talk about Nameless Movement than Nameless (global) Order, as each faction wanted to pull and win <i>their</i> side of narrative. And so the War of Nameless has started in Awakened society.<br /> 4. <b>Post War of Independance</b>, till start of proper Nameless War - Newly recruitated in Revolution and not fully formed young Adamantine Arrows are 'bored' in peaceful live of Awakened now, when all they know is battle magic. When Nameless Movement start to take shape, many of those young Arrows are joining various Nameless factions, just to have excuse to fight with their old Orders siblings and in spite of their previous mentors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-02-2018, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}